  "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nA cross-drill's final clearance point can differ from its feed-entry point by only a few floating-point ULPs. Exact no-motion deduplication then retains a microscopic rapid on some platforms or after moving G54. The deterministic regression produces 14 moves instead of 13 when the stock radius changes from `10.0` to `next_up(10.0)`.\r\n\r\n- Coalesce radial rapid targets only within `1e-9 mm` of the current tip; still call `PathBuilder::push`, so a stationary station/pose change remains real motion.\r\n- Leave the shared CL builder, stock measurements, cutting moves and stock/holder/part safety proofs unchanged.\r\n- Replace opaque raw-float fingerprints with ordered numeric reference chains captured from the pre-fix build. Keep move counts, kinds, feeds and poses strict, and compare only endpoints with a geometric tolerance. Intentionally remove only the captured roundoff-only final rapid.\r\n- Exercise multiple translated G54 positions on both lathe and mill-turn, near-equal radii, real clearance motion and stationary pose indexing.\r\n\r\n## Stack and integration\r\n\r\n**Stacked on #204.** The branch starts at its `efd1f264d0c1924ffed4a5da1b75afee81170e4e` snapshot because both contributions touch `drilling_cross_spindle.rs`. The current parent head `7fff05c665fe4430c8d3633bc946fc7213ae78b6` merged cleanly in a non-worktree-mutating `git merge-tree` preview. That preview is not an executed test of the combined tree; validation below is for this exact contribution head.\r\n\r\nRetarget this PR to `main` **before** merging #204, then refresh/re-gate as required. Human review/merge only; no auto-merge or release is requested.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\nTested/reviewed tree: `4d8bf1feb4319c29da1df62741304ab2c2202269` (commit `f4f277cc2aca9a0515e93f54c3df433a4464482e`).\r\n\r\n- Baseline: `cargo test --locked -j 6 -p camcraft-motion --test cross_invariance` — exit 101, 1 passed / 1 failed; the near-equal-radius case reproduces the extra move. The candidate changes only an assertion-message unit in that fixture, not its executable assertions.\r\n- Candidate: the same command — exit 0, 2 passed / 0 failed.\r\n- `scripts/gate.ps1 -Tier quick -Base efd1f264d0c1924ffed4a5da1b75afee81170e4e` — both selected Cargo steps reported success; 1,150 passed / 0 failed / 17 ignored across 115 libtest result blocks. The canonical map selected motion and app suites, including the complete app suites because of the numeric-reference module. The outer remote wrapper timed out, so its process exit was not captured separately; the gate emitted its complete successful final summary. No wrapper-exit-0 claim is made.\r\n- `cargo clippy --locked -j 6 -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` — exit 0.\r\n- Independent immutable-tree static review — no actionable findings. Commit tree matches the reviewed/tested tree; Cargo.lock unchanged.\r\n\r\n## Limits and readings\r\n\r\n- Native Windows execution only. macOS and Linux x86_64 are not available here. A supplementary Linux aarch64 app-build attempt stopped before tests in unchanged Flecs `c_char` pointer-sign bindings; no dependency workaround is included.\r\n- Repository gates are local; no hosted workflow was enabled or dispatched. Full release/heavy lanes were not requested.\r\n- Readings: issue #151 and its maintainer triage, current `AGENTS.md`/`README.md`, radial generation and spindle/stock/holder/part proof call paths, shared `PathBuilder` semantics and the pre-fix numeric capture. Original synthetic fixtures and elementary floating-point/Euclidean comparison only; no vendor implementation material.\r\n- No new dependencies, data format changes, production NC use or protected-main merge.\r\n\r\nChangelog: Cross-drilling no longer adds a roundoff-only rapid when G54 or platform floating-point results change; preserve station poses and use portable numeric chain regressions.\r\n\r\nFixes #151\r\n",
